WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.375
So what does the code add?

2
00:00:01.375 --> 00:00:04.544
A module, two entry scripts
kept strictly apart,

3
00:00:04.544 --> 00:00:09.338
one that only reads and one that writes,
and its own list of allowed calls.

4
00:00:09.338 --> 00:00:13.181
It builds on Chapter 1's register
and Chapter 3's decisions,

5
00:00:13.181 --> 00:00:16.063
and refuses either if
its hash doesn't match.

6
00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:17.949
Then four reviewed files.

7
00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:22.609
The first gives each re-platformed
account's new account, workload and hosts,

8
00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:27.195
and the SailPoint request and ServiceNow
change that approved its writes;

9
00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:30.375
Chapter 12 writes these
rows for approved requests.

10
00:00:30.375 --> 00:00:33.525
The second says who may
fetch each managed password.

11
00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:38.406
The third is the forest's account standard:
the service account O U, the holding

12
00:00:38.406 --> 00:00:43.287
O U, the creator group, the retriever
group pattern and the thirty-day interval.

13
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:45.850
The fourth is the one program dates file.

14
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.240
The end state has no default:
if the decision is missing,

15
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.480
the run stops rather than guessing.
